      "author": "RuanPienaarCode",
      "description": "The Tax page tracked whether a document existed but never what it said. This release closes that gap and everything that was blocked behind it.\n\n## Figures table\nA third section alongside Progress and Documents, recording the amounts off each certificate by source code — with totals grouped by code, so three banks' interest reads as one line rather than three. Existing tax pages load unchanged; the section simply appears empty until you add to it.\n\n## Checks that read those figures\nCountry profiles now carry `figureChecks()`. The South African profile checks the local-interest exemption, the TFSA annual limit and the capital-gains exclusion, and keeps foreign interest separate from the local-interest test — they are different lines on the return and only local interest is exempt. Thresholds are shown as defaults to verify, not as authority.\n\n## Assessment outcome\nA new **assessed** state, with the assessment's date, reference, result and taxable income. Once those are captured, the page compares the assessed income against what you recorded — and flags an assessment whose taxable income matches your employment income exactly while other income figures were captured, asking whether each was exempt or simply omitted. Two seeded steps were added for South Africa: checking the assessment against your own figures, and deciding on a Request for Correction.\n\n## Upload hygiene\n- Duplicate uploads are now detected by content hash rather than filename, and you are offered the stored file instead of a second copy.\n- A document row can hold several files — providers commonly issue IT3(b), IT3(c) and IT3(s) as separate certificates.\n- Password-protected PDFs are flagged on upload, since Obsidian's viewer cannot open them.\n- Tax year folders with no page behind them are surfaced, so prior-year certificates stop being invisible.\n\n## Install\nManual install: download `main.js`, `manifest.json` and `styles.css` into `<vault>/.obsidian/plugins/budget-app/`, then reload Obsidian.",
